Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/08/31 19:05 SAST
Version: 0.5.8.3
Description:
  Company People section body.

  Lists the people belonging to the company currently in context and offers the three actions a
  company legitimately owns over them: edit the profile fields it manages, disable or enable the
  account, and remove the person from the company.

  Disable and Remove are deliberately separate, and the wording says why. Disabling stops somebody
  signing in and nothing else: membership, enrolments, progress and certificates all remain, so
  enabling returns them to exactly where they were. Removing ends the relationship with this
  company and withdraws the access this company granted, but leaves the person's account and their
  learning history alone. Previously a single Remove action did both, so somebody moving between
  companies was banned from the platform as a side effect and no control existed to reverse it.

  Every action is a POST carrying a CSRF token, and the server decides which company it applies to
  from the session-held context rather than from anything in this markup.

  WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. A comment delimiter
  written inside a comment body ends the comment early and leaks the remainder onto the page.
  Keep every comment plain prose: no comment delimiters and no code, not even to document one.
Changelog:
	2026/08/31 19:05 SAST
	- Round: shared search button moved into noscript, server-search marker on every results region, Course Library rebuilt as paginated accordions, Reports paginated and searched, company requests as a table, company dashboard Courses figure.
  2026/08/29 21:05 SAST
  - Round A. Added Edit, and Disable and Enable as an action distinct from Remove; added the
    account status badge; reindented with tabs and added the required metadata header.
